    "Thus automatic regularity at speed zeros cannot activate the earlier83 sufficient local return-regularity gate. The sufficient implication itself remains valid.",
    "A is factorial without a cancellation assumption. With v=b/g-hs and w=z-bs+qs²/2, both invariant, T=hs²+2vs has z=w+gT/2 and polynomial fixed functions exactly A[T].",
    "The relative presentation B=A[T,S]/(T-hS²-2vS) is finite iff h is a unit, and is finite free of rank2 after h inversion. Proper I forces h nonunit. The global fixed-polynomial intersection is not then a finite-group quotient action on B.",
    "The normalized pair h,v is coprime but may have common zeros. Actual speed zeros are in the linear residue-field branch h=0,v nonzero, not the constant branch h=v=0.",
    "The new actual control has gcd(q,b)=a-1, reduced denominator a³ and return (a,-x-2/a,c,z); it extends across a=1 but not a=0. The retained two-speed control checks the three residue-field cases.",
    "The strict power certificate contracts to I_A in A. Existing inner, natural and continuous closure terminology does not prove polynomial membership. Existing recognition theorems retain actual invariant-coordinate or stable-good-subring premises."
